Problem Statement

1. Duplicate Ticket Sales
Due to the lack of a digital ticket management system, administrators may accidentally overlook seat availability, resulting in the same seat being sold to multiple customers.

2. Poor Booking Record Management
Without a centralized database, administrators may overlook or forget advance booking requests, leading to missed reservations and booking management issues.

3. Inconsistent Ticket Management Procedures
Different administrators may use different methods to record and manage ticket bookings, resulting in inconsistent records, miscommunication, and errors in ticket sales.
